{
  "actors": [
    {
      "id": "analyst",
      "label": "Dashboard",
      "role": "client",
      "x": 14,
      "y": 16
    },
    {
      "id": "coord",
      "label": "Query coordinator",
      "role": "edge",
      "x": 50,
      "y": 16
    },
    {
      "id": "catalog",
      "label": "Catalog and zone maps",
      "role": "data",
      "x": 86,
      "y": 16
    },
    {
      "id": "workers",
      "label": "8 scan workers",
      "role": "compute",
      "x": 50,
      "y": 50
    },
    {
      "id": "store",
      "label": "Object store",
      "role": "data",
      "x": 86,
      "y": 50
    },
    {
      "id": "loader",
      "label": "Loader",
      "role": "async",
      "x": 14,
      "y": 84
    },
    {
      "id": "views",
      "label": "Daily revenue view",
      "role": "data",
      "x": 50,
      "y": 84
    },
    {
      "id": "merge",
      "label": "Merge workers (own a country each)",
      "role": "compute",
      "x": 86,
      "y": 84
    }
  ],
  "frames": [
    {
      "narration": "Earlier today the loader wrote yesterday's last micro-batch. It turned 9 million new order lines into one file per column, sorted by country, and put them in the object store.",
      "messages": [
        {
          "from": "loader",
          "to": "store",
          "label": "column files for 2026-10-10"
        },
        {
          "from": "loader",
          "to": "catalog",
          "label": "commit files, min/max"
        }
      ],
      "states": {
        "catalog": "partition 1,095 added"
      }
    },
    {
      "narration": "A dashboard asks for revenue by country over the last 7 days, for products in one category. It sends SQL to the coordinator, which plans it.",
      "messages": [
        {
          "from": "analyst",
          "to": "coord",
          "label": "sum(amount) by country, 7 days"
        }
      ],
      "states": {
        "coord": "planning"
      }
    },
    {
      "narration": "The coordinator asks the catalog which files can hold the last 7 days. The zone maps rule out 1,088 of the 1,095 daily partitions without reading them.",
      "messages": [
        {
          "from": "coord",
          "to": "catalog",
          "label": "files for 7 days?"
        },
        {
          "from": "catalog",
          "to": "coord",
          "label": "7 of 1,095 partitions"
        }
      ],
      "states": {
        "catalog": "1,088 skipped"
      }
    },
    {
      "narration": "The plan goes to 8 scan workers. Each is given some of the files and reads only 3 columns of the 20: country, product and amount. The small product table is broadcast to every worker so the category filter needs no shuffle.",
      "messages": [
        {
          "from": "coord",
          "to": "workers",
          "label": "plan + product table"
        },
        {
          "from": "workers",
          "to": "store",
          "label": "read 3 of 20 columns"
        }
      ],
      "states": {
        "workers": "scanning 64 million rows"
      }
    },
    {
      "narration": "About 64 million rows and 3 compressed columns come to roughly 0.3 GB, which a cache hit on the workers' SSDs serves in a fraction of a second. Reading all 20 columns of the whole table would have been about 2 TB.",
      "messages": [
        {
          "from": "store",
          "to": "workers",
          "label": "about 0.3 GB, cached after this"
        }
      ],
      "states": {
        "store": "0.3 GB read"
      }
    },
    {
      "narration": "Each scan worker sums its own rows by country, giving a partial result of about 50 rows. The partials are shuffled by a hash of the country to the merge workers, so one worker owns each country and adds up the pieces. Only a few hundred rows cross the network.",
      "messages": [
        {
          "from": "workers",
          "to": "merge",
          "label": "partial sums by country"
        }
      ],
      "states": {
        "workers": "50 partial groups each",
        "merge": "50 groups merged"
      },
      "highlight": [
        "merge"
      ]
    },
    {
      "narration": "The coordinator returns 50 rows, one per country, after about 0.6 seconds.",
      "messages": [
        {
          "from": "merge",
          "to": "coord",
          "label": "50 rows"
        },
        {
          "from": "coord",
          "to": "analyst",
          "label": "result in 0.6 s"
        }
      ],
      "states": {
        "analyst": "chart drawn"
      }
    },
    {
      "narration": "The same dashboard refreshes a minute later, and so do 300 others. Revenue by country by day is a materialised view of a few hundred thousand rows, kept up to date as files arrive. The planner reads the 350 rows for the 7 days and 50 countries from it and never touches the fact table.",
      "messages": [
        {
          "from": "analyst",
          "to": "coord",
          "label": "same query again"
        },
        {
          "from": "coord",
          "to": "views",
          "label": "read 350 rows"
        },
        {
          "from": "views",
          "to": "analyst",
          "label": "result in 40 ms"
        }
      ],
      "states": {
        "views": "350 rows read"
      },
      "highlight": [
        "views"
      ]
    }
  ]
}